1
00:00:01,240 --> 00:00:05,157
A grounded aircraft costs far more than a planned repair.

2
00:00:05,197 --> 00:00:09,440
On this Boeing 787 fleet, nose landing gear actuators

3
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:11,961
are failing more often than expected.

4
00:00:12,001 --> 00:00:15,083
In four months of data, six of ten failed.

5
00:00:15,123 --> 00:00:17,323
AcuMain tells managers which aircraft

6
00:00:17,363 --> 00:00:20,617
will fail in the next thirty days, before it happens.

7
00:00:20,657 --> 00:00:23,147
The dashboard opens with the fleet picture:

8
00:00:23,187 --> 00:00:26,371
how many aircraft are high, medium and low risk,

9
00:00:26,411 --> 00:00:28,009
and one clear alert.

10
00:00:28,049 --> 00:00:31,017
Six aircraft are high risk, and without action

11
00:00:31,057 --> 00:00:33,902
about four of them will fail within thirty days.

12
00:00:33,942 --> 00:00:36,991
The fleet outlook shows how fast the risk is growing:

13
00:00:37,031 --> 00:00:40,916
from no high-risk aircraft in January to six in April.

14
00:00:40,956 --> 00:00:43,043
Every aircraft is ranked by risk,

15
00:00:43,083 --> 00:00:45,676
with a likely range and a clear decision:

16
00:00:45,716 --> 00:00:48,406
schedule repair now, plan an inspection,

17
00:00:48,446 --> 00:00:50,148
or no action needed.

18
00:00:50,188 --> 00:00:52,541
Select any aircraft to see why.

19
00:00:52,581 --> 00:00:57,988
For B787-008, slow operation and very high leakage

20
00:00:58,028 --> 00:01:00,259
drive an eighty-five percent risk,

21
00:01:00,299 --> 00:01:03,683
and its history shows that risk climbing month by month.

22
00:01:03,723 --> 00:01:06,769
Behind it is a model built not to overfit.

23
00:01:06,809 --> 00:01:09,033
Tested on aircraft it had never seen,

24
00:01:09,073 --> 00:01:12,525
it caught six of six failures with one false alarm.

25
00:01:12,565 --> 00:01:15,362
It scores new data the moment it arrives.

26
00:01:15,402 --> 00:01:18,093
Fewer surprise groundings. Better planning.

27
00:01:18,133 --> 00:01:20,217
More aircraft ready to fly.

28
00:01:20,257 --> 00:01:23,122
AcuMain: predict the failure before it happens.
